  "notes": "MADLIB  (Madvillainy, Jaylib, the beat tapes)\n\nTECHNIQUE (sourced)\n- \"I did most of the Madvillain album in Brazil... in my hotel room... on a portable\n  turntable, my (Boss SP) 303, and a little tape deck.\" He also names the Roland SP-606 and\n  likes it for its effects (Scratch via Stones Throw, 2005).\n- An SP-404 on Madvillainy is impossible: it came out in 2005, after the album.\n\nTHIS TEMPLATE\nSP-303 Sampler, quantize off, Lo-Fi grade (press Vinyl Sim for compression, noise and wow).\nA loose drum rack swung at 56%: The drum rack plays one-shots synthesized for these templates (CC0, no recordings), in the voice of the machine each channel is named for, with a starter beat in the pattern; replace them with your own samples for the real machine. Voice Drops on a second Sampler (SP Pitch).\n\nWORKFLOW\nLoops long and loose; chop by ear, play pads in live, keep the mistakes. Record a pass to\nthe master's tape chain and decide later.\n\nMIX NOTES\n- Drum Bus: a hard built-in compressor, CHOWTapeModel \"Lofi Vibe\". Music Bus: CHOWTapeModel\n  \"Dirtier Cassette\".\n- Master: CHOWTapeModel \"Dirtier Cassette\", -2 dB shelf, Lemon Limiter; -13 to -10 LUFS.\n- Loudness: streaming plays back near -14 LUFS integrated (Spotify), so a louder master is turned down; keep true peak below -1 dBTP.\n\nCOVERAGE\nStrong for the SP-303 workflow. Weak: no SP-606 model; the drums are synthesized one-shots, not samples of the machines.\n\nSOURCES\nStones Throw \"Mad Skills\" (Scratch Magazine, 2005); MusicTech SP-303 feature; Spotify for Artists, \"Loudness normalization\" (support.spotify.com/us/artists/article/loudness-normalization).\n\nFREE PLUG-INS (download them before opening the template; a missing one keeps its slot)\n- OB-Xf (GPL-3.0): https://github.com/surge-synthesizer/OB-Xf\n- CHOWTapeModel (GPL-3.0): https://chowdsp.com/products.html\n\nSETUP (written from this template)\nTempo 92 BPM, 4/4, key Gmin, cycle bars 1-4.\n\nTracks\n- Chops (SP-303) (Instrument, +0 dB) -> Music Bus\n    instrument: Sampler (SP-303 model): no effect; quantize oFF; pad grade lofi\n- Drums (Instrument, +0 dB) -> Drum Bus\n    instrument: Channel Rack (synthesized one-shots of the template samples: Kick = kick-acoustic.wav, Snare = snare-acoustic.wav, Closed Hat = hat-acoustic.wav, Open Hat = openhat-acoustic.wav, Rim = rim.wav, Shaker = shaker.wav)\n    region: Step Sequencer pattern with a starter beat (13 steps on), swing 56% (MPC terms), 6 rows = the rack's channels\n- Bass / Organ (Instrument, -10 dB) -> Music Bus\n    instrument: Surge Synth Team: OB-Xf: OB-Xf patch \"Organs/Transistorg\"\n- Voice Drops (Instrument, -8 dB) -> Music Bus\n    instrument: Sampler (SP-303 model): effect Pitch on, CTRL 1-3 = 60%, 0%, 100%; quantize oFF; pad grade lofi\n\nBuses (the n-th Aux strip listens to bus n)\n- Drum Bus (bus 1): chowdsp: CHOWTapeModel: factory preset \"Lofi Vibe\"; Compressor (Threshold -24, Ratio 8, Attack 1, Release 80, Make-up 6)\n- Music Bus (bus 2): chowdsp: CHOWTapeModel: factory preset \"Dirtier Cassette\"\n- Vocal Bus (bus 3): empty\n- Reverb (bus 4): Space D (Size 140, Dry -96, Wet 0, Decay 1, Decay Curve 1, IR \"00.5s Small Room\")\n- Delay (bus 5): Tape Delay (Time 326.1, Feedback 0.5, Tone 3000, Mix 1)\n\nStereo Out\n- built-in effects: Channel EQ (High -2); Compressor (Threshold -14, Ratio 2, Attack 30, Release 200)\n- plug-ins (after the built-in effects): chowdsp: CHOWTapeModel: factory preset \"Dirtier Cassette\"; Lemon Limiter: gain +2 dB, ceiling -1 dB, other settings default\n\nBring your own samples: no recordings are included.\n",
